waila.item.panascais_caves:the_deep_mistake_scroll=Pergamino del error profundo\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7They tunneled where no dwarf dared before.\nThe pick struck stone, but the stone bled\nblack. The mountain trembled and this was\nthe first breath "IT" took in millennia.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_binding_scroll=Pergamino de la atadura\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Five mages stood beneath the mountain's\nheart, hands trembling with grief. What\nthey forged was not art, but\nwarding-sigils drawn from pain, hammered\ninto silence.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_scattering_scroll=Pergamino de la dispersion\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7One beast, five wards. To keep it\ndreaming, the sigils were shattered and\nburied in places no map names-where frost\ngnaws, fires weep, and nothing speaks.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_glyphs_scroll=Pergamino de los glifos\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7A stone altar listens beneath the world.\nFive marks wait-not for touch, but memory.\nThe matching must be true, or the silence\ndeepens.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_awakening_scroll=Pergamino del despertar\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Piedra cracks. polvo breathes. The altar\ngroans beneath ancient weight. When the\nfifth mark finds its place, The Serpent\nstirs. Coils unwind, eyes open without\nlight, and the mountain forgets its\nsilence.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_flame_scroll=Pergamino de la prueba de la llama\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7In the lakes that blaze and howl, Ember\nwaits behind walls of living fire. Only\nthe worthy walk unscorched-their path\ncools where others burn.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_water_scroll=Pergamino de la prueba del agua\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Water hides where ice breathes blue and\nlight bends twice. Align the mirrors to\nreveal its shape-only perfect stillness\nsees what's real.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_wind_scroll=Pergamino de la prueba del viento\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Wind drifts among open roots and quiet\nrivers. It does not lie still- follow the\nbreeze, and step where silence welcomes\nyou.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_earth_scroll=Pergamino de la prueba de la tierra\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Buried in the earth, beneath dust and\ngemlight. amatista spires and broken\ndeserts hold its shape. Only the\nheavy-hearted may lift it.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:whispers_of_the_forgemaster_scroll=Pergamino de los susurros del maestro forjador\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7It cleaves stone, splits timber, and\ncarves paths no other tool dares-\nRunebreaker, the Forgemaster's last\ncreation. Not forged to fight, but to\nshape the world itself. The runes bend to\nits will. The mountain remembers its name.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:lost_in_collapse_scroll=Pergamino perdido en el derrumbe\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7When the serpent was sealed away and the\nmountains fell silent, all records of the\nRunebreaker vanished. Some say it lies\nburied beneath the beast itself in the\nshattered altar, waiting for a soul bold\nenough to dig deep.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:facets_of_power_scroll=Pergamino de las facetas del poder\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Six gemstones-zafiro, esfalerita,\nEmerald, rubi, opalo cristalino, and onice-\neach forged as a fragment of dwarven\nmastery. Only when gathered can the\nancient tool be touched.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:runes_in_stone_scroll=Pergamino de runas en la piedra\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7The serpent bears five wounds hidden\nbeneath petrified coil. When it falls,\nthey open... and the gemstones call out.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_forgotten_trial_scroll=Pergamino de la prueba olvidada\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7En la arboleda olvidada por el tiempo, las\nrunas duermen bajo reliquias derruidas. Lo\nque el mundo olvida, el tiempo espera con\npaciencia a quienes buscan lo perdido.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_runebreaker_scroll=Pergamino del Rompirrunas\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Inserta las seis gemas en lo que oculta la\nserpiente, y la montana respondera. La\nreliquia despertara. No con llamas ni acero\n- sino con un poder largo tiempo negado.\n§r§r
